[{:seon.task/name "a-stalled-eval-ends-with-its-error", :seon.task/plan "Found by context, 2026-11-13 (notes: evidence/context-refine-hang-2026-11-13.md): a refine's turn-9 eval ran grep -rl over its checkout and blocked in open(2) for 80 minutes; the agent proc recorded it :stalled {:quiet-ms .. :last-op {:kind :tests}}, and nothing ended the eval or answered it with an error, so the run waited until a person ended the grep. Nothing may hang (docs/errors.md#nothing-crashes-and-nothing-hangs): a stalled eval is ended, its child processes with it, and answered with a typed error naming what it waited on, so the turn goes on and the agent reads why. Owner: runtime (the stall in seon.agent-proc, its answer in seon.system's back-op). Proof: an eval whose child blocks forever (a read of a FIFO no one writes) is answered with that error, and the agent's next eval runs. Plan (root's yes 2026-11-13, with its notes): (1) an eval's own bound: stated by its request (a test run's: its tests' recorded times x :seon.config.proofs/stall-factor), else measured for its kind (its :last-op kind; :seon.config.check/step-end-factor times that kind's median wall time on this root, the medians derived from the evals' own facts in the store, never an atom, floored at the factor times the kind's floor); a tick bound cannot see a wait (a child in open(2) spends no ticks). The agent proc holds each request's bound and observes the stall past it: one :seon.agent/stalled naming the bound; the api's :stall-check timer and stall-ms go (task seon.system/a-stall-is-past-the-requests-own-bound). (2) Evidence before anything ends: bin/evidence's capture of the agent's process tree (ps, lsof, sample, SIGINFO dumps) into its runs dir, the path riding the error. (3) The end: the eval's children killed (a test child ends by its own wall bound), the eval answered :seon.agent/stalled-wait {:bound :waited-ms :kind :evidence :children}, never retried; the turn goes on. Proofs, red first: seon.procs-test/a-stall-is-observed-past-the-requests-own-bound; seon.agent-test/a-stalled-eval-is-answered-with-its-error (a child reading a FIFO nobody writes, a short stated bound, answered with an evidence path holding its lsof; a busy eval below its bound untouched). Completes seon.system/a-stall-is-past-the-requests-own-bound too. Estimate: a pure step test ~1M, one in-agent run ~3M; per stall one capture (~1-2 s) once.", :seon.task/kind :work, :seon.task/proofs #{seon.agent-test/a-stalled-eval-is-answered-with-its-error}}]
